From 66bb73df79012e52cb538c76d47ca51153ff0504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Neuhaus <thomas.neuhaus1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:56:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mlinux: fix premature CFG80211_VERSION_CODE>=7.0.0
 wireless_dev gate

The driver gates several cfg80211 station-management call sites
(cfg80211_new_sta/cfg80211_del_sta, add_station/change_station/
del_station ops, IEEE80211_MIN_ACTION_SIZE usage) on
'CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 0, 0)' to select a
wireless_dev-based API this driver revision expects future mainline
kernels to adopt at that version. As of Linux 7.0.0 (this board's
kernel, linux-kiss), mainline cfg80211 has NOT made that change -
cfg80211_new_sta()/cfg80211_del_sta() and the station cfg80211_ops
callbacks still take struct net_device *, and IEEE80211_MIN_ACTION_SIZE
is still a plain (non-parameterized) macro. Building against a real
7.0.0 kernel therefore fails with incompatible-pointer-type errors.

Bump the gate to KERNEL_VERSION(99, 0, 0) (never true for now) so the
driver falls back to its net_device-based / legacy code paths, which
match the actual current mainline API. Revisit/remove this once
mainline genuinely adopts the wireless_dev-based station API and
CFG80211_VERSION_CODE reflects the kernel that ships it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local workaround for a downstream-only
version-gate assumption, not applicable to nxp-imx/mwifiex.git upstream
until real mainline cfg80211 adopts the wireless_dev station API]
---
 mlinux/moal_cfg80211.c     | 12 ++++++------
 mlinux/moal_cfg80211.h     | 10 +++++-----
 mlinux/moal_shim.c         |  4 ++--
 mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------
 mlinux/moal_uap_cfg80211.c |  6 +++---
 5 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

